 "schema": "pcc.claim/v1",
 "scope": "Actual coordinate ring over a field K; explicit nonsingularity, injective abscissas, nonzero pair, norm-degree or component caps; scalar order q prime separate from K;13 maintained laws and4 symbolic applications; no numerical/native qualification execution or independent signed PCC verdict.",
 "statement": "Supplied nonzero tight rows on actual nonsingular short-Weierstrass points with distinct abscissas produce a principal point-ideal product, actual group sum zero, and prime-order mixed-label recovery when the second-label sum is nonzero. Local all-tracked source audit exits0 at684/0/0; fast discovery, original useful yield and the complete classical subexponential ECDLP criterion remain open. Separate literature screen and translation-folding plans are prospective, not implemented selectors."
